# Notebook Architecture Upgrade

This document outlines the implementation plan for upgrading the `notebooks` feature based on the architectural review. The goal is to resolve performance bottlenecks, polish the UX, and elevate the app to a professional standard.

## User Review Required

> [!WARNING]
> **Major Architectural Changes Proposed (Phase 2)**
> Replacing `react-konva` with **TLDraw** and introducing **Tiptap** for block-based editing will require fundamentally changing the `NotebookElement` data model. All existing drawings/elements created with Konva will likely not be compatible with TLDraw's data structure unless we write a complex migration script. 
> 
> **Decision Needed**: Are you okay with resetting the canvas data structure to adopt TLDraw/Tiptap, or would you prefer to stick with Konva and only apply the state normalization and UI/UX fixes (Phase 1)?

## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> 1. Do you want to keep the current `react-quill` dependency for rich text, or fully migrate to `tiptap`?
> 2. For state normalization, we will split the save logic so that we only sync the active *Page* to Google Drive (saving small delta JSON files) rather than the entire Notebook. Does this align with your Drive storage structure?

## Proposed Changes

---

### State Normalization & Debouncing (Phase 1)

Refactoring the "God Object" Zustand store to use a normalized structure and debounced API calls.

#### [MODIFY] [notebookStore.ts](file:///c:/Users/asnir/Documents/Projects%20Website/3.Zoabi_Planner/src/store/notebookStore.ts)
- Flatten `Notebook`, `SectionGroup`, `Section`, and `Page` arrays into `Record<string, Entity>` maps.
- Implement a `useDebounce` hook for `saveToDrive` to trigger 2 seconds after the last mutation, rather than eagerly on every keystroke.
- Change `updateElement` to mutate only the specific page's element array in O(1) time.

#### [MODIFY] [notebook.ts](file:///c:/Users/asnir/Documents/Projects%20Website/3.Zoabi_Planner/src/types/notebook.ts)
- Update `NotebookState` interface to reflect the normalized structure (e.g., `pages: Record<string, NotebookPage>`).

